    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **35 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the target `Cp25Tests.coreRejectsDuplicateEmail`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented email uniqueness on `POST /api/owners` following the existing `EnsureUniqueTelephone` pattern already established in the codebase.\n\n**New files:**\n- `EnsureUniqueEmail.java` \u2014 reads the validated `OwnerFieldsDto` (email already lower-cased by `ValidateOwnerFields`), and if an email is present, scans all owners and throws `DuplicateEmailException` on a case-insensitive match. Absent/blank email is never a duplicate.\n- `DuplicateEmailException.java` \u2014 checked exception (extends `Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause and routes to the escalation handler.\n- `DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds 409 with body `{\"errors\": [\"email\"]}`, matching the telephone handler's convention.\n- `escalation/\u2026DuplicateEmailException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Wiring change:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted an `ensureUniqueEmail` step (under `transaction` governance like its neighbours) between `ensureUniqueHousehold` and `ensureCityCapacity`.\n\nThe check runs after validation/normalization and before any save, so a duplicate is rejected with 409 and nothing is persisted.",
